  'cmjamdqj2000fw9005h321idg', 'Optimize a Child Component with React.memo', 'The `React.memo` higher-order component (HOC) is used to optimize functional components. It works by memoizing the rendered output of a component and only re-rendering it when its props have shallowly changed. In this scenario, by wrapping `MyItem` with `React.memo`, React will perform a shallow comparison of the `id` and `name` props between renders. If they are the same (which they are when only the parent''s `count` state changes), `MyItem` will skip its own render, thus improving performance by preventing unnecessary work.', 'You are given a React application with a `ParentComponent` that renders a list of `MyItem` components. The `ParentComponent` has a state `count` that updates when a button is clicked. When the `count` updates, the `ParentComponent` re-renders, which in turn causes all `MyItem` components to re-render, even though their `id` and `name` props haven''t changed. This leads to unnecessary re-renders and potential performance issues.

Your task is to optimize the `MyItem` functional component using `React.memo` to prevent it from re-rendering when its props (`id`, `name`) remain unchanged. You only need to provide the modified `MyItem` component code.', 'easy', ARRAY['React performance optimization', 'React.memo', 'Functional Components'], 'coding', 'import React from ''react'';

const MyItem = React.memo(({ id, name }) => {
  // This console.log would demonstrate fewer re-renders after optimization
  // console.log(`Rendering MyItem ${id}`); 
  return (
    <li>
      {name} (ID: {id})
    </li>
  );
});

export default MyItem;', '[{"input":"import React from ''react'';\n\nconst MyItem = ({ id, name }) => {\n  // In a real application, a console.log here would show frequent re-renders\n  return (\n    <li>\n      {name} (ID: {id})\n    </li>\n  );\n};\n\nexport default MyItem;","output":"import React from ''react'';\n\nconst MyItem = React.memo(({ id, name }) => {\n  // With React.memo, this should log less frequently if props don''t change\n  return (\n    <li>\n      {name} (ID: {id})\n    </li>\n  );\n});\n\nexport default MyItem;"}]', NULL, NULL, '', 'approved', 'system', TRUE, 'library_ai_coding', '2025-12-17T23:05:28.718Z', '2025-12-17T23:05:29.024Z', TRUE, FALSE, NULL, NULL, TRUE, 'cmjamdqj2000fw9005h321idg', NULL
